=== sort() Function with Key Parameter Tests ===

1. Reverse sort (negate number):
   Original:  [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]
   Original unchanged:  [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]
   Sorted result (descending):  [9, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 1]

2. String length sort:
   Original:  ["zebra", "apple", "banana", "cherry", "a", "hello", "hi"]
   Original unchanged:  ["zebra", "apple", "banana", "cherry", "a", "hello", "hi"]
   Sorted result (by length):  ["a", "hi", "zebra", "apple", "hello", "banana", "cherry"]

3. Reverse string length sort:
   Original:  ["a", "hi", "hello", "apple", "banana", "zebra"]
   Original unchanged:  ["a", "hi", "hello", "apple", "banana", "zebra"]
   Sorted result (by length, descending):  ["banana", "hello", "apple", "zebra", "hi", "a"]

4. Mixed numbers - reverse sort:
   Original:  [10, 2, 8, 1, 9, 5, 3]
   Original unchanged:  [10, 2, 8, 1, 9, 5, 3]
   Sorted result (descending):  [10, 9, 8, 5, 3, 2, 1]

5. String length sort with same lengths:
   Original:  ["cat", "dog", "bat", "rat", "a", "z", "hi", "go"]
   Original unchanged:  ["cat", "dog", "bat", "rat", "a", "z", "hi", "go"]
   Sorted result (by length):  ["a", "z", "hi", "go", "cat", "dog", "bat", "rat"]

6. Using a named function for key:
   Original:  [5, 2, 8, 1, 9]
   Original unchanged:  [5, 2, 8, 1, 9]
   Sorted result (using negate function):  [9, 8, 5, 2, 1]

7. String length using named function:
   Original:  ["hello", "a", "world", "hi", "test"]
   Original unchanged:  ["hello", "a", "world", "hi", "test"]
   Sorted result (using str_len function):  ["a", "hi", "test", "hello", "world"]

8. Empty array with key function:
   Original:  []
   Sorted result:  []

9. Single element with key function:
   Original:  [42]
   Sorted result:  [42]

=== All sort() with Key Parameter Tests Complete ===
